      "<p>Troy University is a public University comprising a network of campuses throughout Alabama and globally. Founded in 1887 as Troy State Normal School within the Alabama State University System, it is now a powerhouse of higher education. More than 1000 International Students enrol at Troy University every year.</p><p>International in its focus, Troy University offers a range of undergraduate courses that include Global Business Management, Cybersecurity, Human Resource Management and more.</p> <p>The Learning Center provides free tutoring, study groups, and peer academic skills coaching for Troy University enrolled students. The Troy University Libraries are vast and well-stocked, with access provided to 250+ databases so students can easily find learning materials on campus. The career services team makes a concerted effort to help students with CV reviews, cover letters and interview techniques so they are well-positioned to find graduate work. The athletics facilities at Troy University span across different sports disciplines, with multiple arenas: the Troy soccer complex, Lunsford tennis complex, Troy softball complex, Troy golf practice facility, the Trojan arena, Riddle-pace field, and Veterans memorial stadiums.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Troy University is known as Alabamaâ€™s International University and as such, student life at Troy University is celebrative of its rich multicultural student body. Troy University is home to more than 150 student organisations in academic, cultural, sports and other fields. From Greek life to special interest societies such as The Swing Dance Club or the Board Game Alliance, there is lots of activity occurring on campus. 200+ Annual Fine Arts Performances occur on campus throughout the year. The Dining Service on the Troy University campus provides fresh food and a range of dietary options in its Trojan Dining Hall with five wildly different food stations. The 300-seat Adams Center Performing Arts Theatre is situated on the second floor of the Trojan Center and often shows drama performances.</p> <p>Troy is a small student town located in the world-famous state of Alabama. A historic downtown area that paints a picturesque image perfect for studying combines with a multitude of museums so international students can get acquainted with everyday American life. Troy, Alabama is known for its scenery on account of its Southern American location, with Pike Country Lake and the Heart of Dixie Trail Ride providing leisurely downtime activities for students at Troy University. Hearty Southern fried chicken can be found at the local Trojan Bar &amp; Grill, with the Sips Beer Garden &amp; Food Court and â€˜Sips on the Squareâ€™ pizzeria restaurant both offering great opportunities for socialising amongst locals.</p>"
